course: dictionary
lesson: 6719
title: Official: approved, formal and real
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Official» means approved by people in charge, like a government, a school or an organisation. An official passport is one that the government has made and checked. When you meet the word, ask: does it mean approved by the right people?
explain: «Official» can also mean done as part of a job or in a formal way. «The referee made an official decision after the goal.» The referee is in charge of the game, so the decision counts under the rules, and everyone must accept it.
explain: An official is a person with an important job in an organisation, like a referee or a government worker. Be careful: a fake message can look official, with a big logo and grand words. Check whether it really comes from the official website, then decide if you trust it.
fact: Official means approved by people in charge, like a government, school or organisation.
fact: Official also means done as part of a job or in a formal way.
fact: An official is a person with an important job in an organisation, like a referee or an umpire.
fact: Official documents include passports and birth certificates.
fact: Official languages are the languages a country uses for law and government.
exercise: «Only buy codes and currency from an official shop, because strangers often sell fake ones.» What does official shop mean? | A shop with a loud sign | A shop that is closed on Sundays | * A shop that is approved and run by the real company | A cheap shop run by a stranger
exercise: Which of these is an official document? | * A birth certificate | A shopping list | A comic book | A football sticker
exercise: Which person is an official? | A fan cheering in the stands | A child eating a snack on the sideline | A player who scores a goal | * A referee who enforces the rules of a match
test: «Before you trust a message, check whether it comes from the official website.» What should you do first? | Share it with all your friends straight away | * Find the real official website and check the information there | Click every link to see where it goes | Believe it because it has a big logo
test: What is an official language? | A language used only in nursery rhymes | * A language a country uses for law and government | A language that no one has ever spoken | A secret language made up by children
exam: Which sentence uses official to mean done as part of a job or in a formal way? | «The dog ran off to play in the park.» | «The sun was warm and bright over the hills.» | «We ate pizza on Friday.» | * «The referee made an official decision after the goal.»
